      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-olive">Who You&rsquo;d Be Working With</p>
      <h2 class="display">I seek to step into the trenches with you.</h2>
      <p>I believe healing begins when another person bears witness to our deepest fears, hopes, and longings, and that most of us are carrying unconscious patterns that quietly shape our relationships and keep us stuck in cycles of disconnection. My work is to help you untangle those patterns, at a pace that feels safe, in a style that gets right to the point.</p>
      <p>I&rsquo;m trained in Emotionally Focused Therapy (EFT), currently in my second year of formal training in ISTDP (Intensive Short-Term Dynamic Psychotherapy), and informed by attachment work.</p>
      <p class="credential">Anne Warner, Associate Marriage &amp; Family Therapist, AMFT #150232 &middot; Supervised by Susan Beisner, LMFT #46150, and Dr. Michele Willingham, PSY #15849</p>
